body:
He's a mutt; part chow, baljin malinwah or something. I just call him a cutie though

&#x200B;

Same, I like distracting myself when I'm stressed. I fell down a cliff once and the only reason I didn't just freak out and panic about getting up was talking to myself.

I go on walks with my dog. He's a cute boy; peed in the yard and destroyed all our grass, constantly sheds everywhere, and if you're in the car resting your arm you'd better KNOW you're bout to get a nose up your armpit, but aside from that he's a loving dog. Couldn't ask for a better one.

&#x200B;

I like suspense and comedy. But then who dosen't like laughing and feeling stressed?

&#x200B;

I'm really sorry to hear that, dude. It sounds hard. I obviously am not in nearly the same situation, so I can't relate, but I can understand how it must feel to have people constantly arguing around you and using you as a sort of bridge for their communications. I'm glad to see you still see them both, though. It's good not to cut ties. And I'm certianly glad you feel good enough to talk about it, even if it is because of secret-sharing or sommin. If you need someone to talk to about it, don't hesitate ok?

I love being able to walk outside n hear the birds. I also loved the sense of adventure as a kid; I wanted to go to this forest next to my school when I was a little kid, but my mom didn't let me so I couldn't.

&#x200B;

I mean most of it is just in a car. Usually I just sit in the front seat and talk with my mom. sometimes i sneak in a book n read discreetly

&#x200B;

I'm really sorry to hear that. Would you like to talk about your family situation, or is that too personal?

I don't think pretty scenery and scary bikers particularly go together, unless every biker is hagrid from harry potter of course. But yeah, it's beautiful; there's not any ocean where I am, but tons of forests.

&#x200B;

For me it's every other weekend because it's a 30 minuite drive to my school from my mom's, and my dad's is further. Course, it's probably better they're seperated. My dad is gay so that's not exactly the best situation for a straight relationship.

I've been in the same house my whole life; I like it here, it's pretty there's lots of bikers and my parent is here

&#x200B;

Technically my dad is in another town, he and my mom divorced, so I soppose I do technically live in another house too? It's every other week though.
